From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:38:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 19/24] board: mediatek-mobile: reserve LK's regions in LMB
 before EFI init

A saved console record showed a synchronous abort in efi_allocate_pool()
at 0x33ffff000: efi_memory_init() runs right after initr_lmb() and picked
the top page of DRAM, which lies in LK's no-map dramc-rk1 region that
U-Boot leaves unmapped, because the LK reservations were only added in
misc_init_r(). Register banks and reservations in lmb_arch_add_memory()
(LMB_ARCH_MEM_MAP) instead.

Also drop the T880's legacy mediatek,ssusb child, which U-Boot's mtu3
glue rejects ("legacy mediatek,ssusb child is unsupported").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/dts/mt6897-alldocube-t880.dts        |  3 +++
 arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Kconfig                |  1 +
 .../mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c         | 25 +++++++++++++++----
 3 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/mt6897-alldocube-t880.dts b/arch/arm/dts/mt6897-alldocube-t880.dts
index 48b2505e39a..73b18f32fda 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/mt6897-alldocube-t880.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/mt6897-alldocube-t880.dts
@@ -82,6 +82,9 @@
 
 /delete-node/ &usbphy;
 
+/* U-Boot's mtu3 glue rejects the legacy ssusb child; device mode needs none. */
+/delete-node/ &ssusb;
+
 &ufshci {
 	compatible = "mediatek,mt6897-ufshci";
 	reg = <0x112b0000 0x3000>;
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Kconfig b/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Kconfig
index e38c98e0c28..e6fd1394763 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Kconfig
@@ -193,6 +193,7 @@ config TARGET_MEDIATEK_MOBILE
 	select OF_BOARD_FIXUP
 	select OF_BOARD_SETUP
 	select ARMV8_CNTFRQ_BROKEN
+	select LMB_ARCH_MEM_MAP
 	select POSITION_INDEPENDENT
 	select SAVE_PREV_BL_FDT_ADDR
 	select SAVE_PREV_BL_INITRAMFS_START_ADDR
diff --git a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
index 8a604603338..377852df258 100644
--- a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
+++ b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
@@ -705,20 +705,35 @@ static void mtk_find_payload(void)
 	unmap_sysmem(base);
 }
 
-int misc_init_r(void)
+/*
+ * LMB memory: LK's banks minus its reservations, registered before the EFI
+ * memory map is built from LMB (efi_memory_init runs right after
+ * initr_lmb); otherwise EFI pools land in no-map regions U-Boot does not
+ * map. ft_board_setup() reads LK's FDT again and the payload search reads
+ * the initrd, so those stay reserved as well.
+ */
+void lmb_arch_add_memory(void)
 {
-	phys_addr_t fastboot;
 	int i;
 
-	mtk_trace("U-Boot: misc_init_r\n");
-	mtk_pstore_console();
+	for (i = 0; i < mtk_bank_count; i++)
+		lmb_add(mtk_banks[i].start, mtk_banks[i].size);
 	for (i = 0; i < mtk_reserved_count; i++)
 		mtk_reserve(mtk_reserved[i].start, mtk_reserved[i].size,
 			    mtk_reserved[i].nomap ? LMB_NOMAP : LMB_NOOVERWRITE);
-	/* ft_board_setup() reads LK's FDT again; keep it and the initrd intact. */
 	mtk_reserve(mtk_lk_fdt, mtk_lk_fdt_size, LMB_NOOVERWRITE);
 	mtk_reserve(mtk_initrd_start, mtk_initrd_end - mtk_initrd_start,
 		    LMB_NOOVERWRITE);
+	mtk_trace("U-Boot: LMB has %d banks and %d LK reservations\n",
+		  mtk_bank_count, mtk_reserved_count);
+}
+
+int misc_init_r(void)
+{
+	phys_addr_t fastboot;
+
+	mtk_trace("U-Boot: misc_init_r\n");
+	mtk_pstore_console();
 
 	mtk_set_serial();
 	mtk_find_payload();
-- 
2.55.0

